/////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 1. Capacity to Contract : I affirm that I am of the age of majority and possess the legal capacity to contract. Denial of my access to principal credit based on an inability to obtain a consumer credit score constitutes age discrimination. Specifically, do you deny my ability to enter into a valid contract solely based on age discrimination? This practice unjustly penalizes me based on my age or age of credit rather than my qualifications. Denying credit based on a lack of a credit score may disproportionately affect certain groups if those groups generally have less access to traditional credit.

Furthermore, the lack of alternative methods for credit approval exacerbates this discrimination.

If you dispute this claim, can you provide the justification for such a position?

What factors influenced your decision to deny my credit application rather than considering my qualifications and financial profile?

/////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 2. Application Mismanagement : It has come to my attention that my application may have been treated as security collateral without providing me any benefit.

